* PFMSYS -  Geneve OS loader for PFM512 device
*           Loader is independent of MDOS embedded CRC (unlike CYA)
*
*  1998   - original program LOADPFM
* 9.9.2018  Updated to work with Atmel 040a; must add product ID code
*           Consider adding support for other chips
*           Incorporated PRODID (prodids) routine
*
* 9.10.2018
*   This program now performs the following steps:
*      1. Load OS into memory
*      2. Check embedded MDOS CRC
*      3. Tell user status [pass/fail] then ask permission to update
*      4. Program or exit
*      5. Validate
*
*   The MDOS embedded CRC is NOT the same as the PFM embedded CRC
*      1. MDOS embedded CRC calculates all 16 banks, is inverted, and
*         skips the bytes in bank #4 corresponding to the CRC itself
*      2. PFM core CRC calculates the first 15 banks only, does NOT skip
*         the embedded MDOS crc bytes. Therefore, we must calculate bank 4
*         twice.
*
*  Left To Do :
*      1. Update PFM512 loader  [COMPLETE 9.11.2018]
*      2. Write utility to save OS from PFM to disk
*      3. Update PFM CORE programmer for cross-chip compatibility
;
;
;3.20.2021  Reviewed code; some issues with the tables.
;           Plan: use pages FE and FF for 136K MDOS.
;
;      ---> COPY files around line 550
;
;3.26.2021  Modified 040 V7 core: eliminated product ID and CRC
;           Simplified PFMSYS by removing CRC writing
;      $$$$ Add code to test for wire fault (compare 4 banks)
;
;4.2.2021   Removed long crc displays.
;
;03.15.2024 Now using common (CRCMAINS) routines
; v1.6      Fixed ttyout routine
